@using System.Text.RegularExpressions
@using Validated.Core.Types

@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_Path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Inputs}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_TimeInput}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Overview_Tests}")]

@inject ILiveRegionService _liveRegionService

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Time_Input @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview_Tests</PageTitle>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class @GlobalValues.Info_Box_Coloured_Modifier">
    <h1 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Time_Input @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview_Tests</h1>

    <p>
        The Time Input component in this library is a composite component using ARIA <span>role="group"</span> and combines a label for the composite component, an optional area for hint text, with time segment labels and inputs 
        for each time segment, Hours, Minutes and an optional Seconds segment. Finally with a region below the inputs for validation messages. 
    </p>

</section>


<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class">

    <h2 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Information & instructions</h2>
    <p>
        The examples below only use two fields, <b>Start Time</b> (non nullable, required) field and <b>Start Work</b> an optional (nullable, can be left blank) field. Both have the same validation rule attached
        stipulating that the entry must be between 7am and 10am for the Start Time, but only if an entry is made for the Start Work field.        
    </p>
    <p>
        For these example rather than use a red asterisk next to the label and the <span class="code-span">aria-required</span> attribute to indicate that the Start Time field is required, I opted to place the text
        "Required" at the start of the hint text.
    </p>
    <p>
        For the examples the following Validation Display options are used in each test so you can test the options with your chosen devices.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            Described By With Hint -  This options links the time input (group) to the hint text via the <span class="code-span">aria-describedby</span> attribute. The id of unordered list element that holds any validation errors
            is added or removed from the <span class="code-span">aria-describedby</span> attribute, depending on the validity of the value. The id of the validation errors element is places first in the attribute.
        </li>
        <li>
            Described By Hint Suppressed - This option removes the id of the hint text element from the <span class="code-span">aria-describedby</span> attribute when there are validation errors to reduce verbosity
            for screen reader users.
        </li>
        <li>
            Tabbable With Hint - This option only uses the <span class="code-span">aria-describedby</span> attribute for the hint text element which is never removed. The Validation errors area is given a tab stop
            and is promoted to a landmark regions. In the following examples these transient regions will have the accessible name of [Label Text] + " errors" so for the "Start Time" field the region would be "Start Time errors".
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        For each of the above options there are two examples, one that uses Blazors <span class="code-span">oninput</span> event which causes validation on every keystroke the other using the <span class="code-span">onchange</span> event
        which occurs if the value has changed and once focus is lost - in this instance when focus is moved from the time input group component.
    </p>
    <p>
        Examples one to three use the "On Input" event whilst examples four to six use the "On Change" event.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Important: </strong>Unlike the non-composite inputs where some screen reader/browser combinations treat the <span class="code-span">aria-describedby</span> attribute similar to a live region, with the 
        <span class="code-span">role="group"</span> in play this behaviour is not exhibited.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Note: </strong>Given the myriad combinations of screen reader, operating system, browser, validation display option and event used, I have not provided an expectations section like the tests for other components. My preferred option given
        that the behaviour is the same for all is to use the tabbable region option with the "oninput" event, but you should choose the options that best suit your target audience.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Examples using oninput (immediate validation)</h2>
    
    <section class="section-box">
        <h3>Example one - fake form using the option "Described By With Hint" and the "On Input" event.</h3>

        <EditForm EditContext="@_editContextOne" OnSubmit="HandleSubmitOne">
        
            <BlazorValidated TEntity="ScheduleDto" BoxedValidators="_boxedValidators" AddDisplayName="true" />

            <div class="br-input-row">
                <TimeInput class="br-col-xs-12 br-col-sm-6" LabelText="Start Time" @bind-Value="@_scheduleDataOne.StartTime" HintText="Required, the time (24-hour format) you want the scheduled action to start."
                           Required="false" EnableSeconds="true" DataPosition="DataPosition.Start" UpdateOnInput="true" ParseErrorMessage="Must be a valid time."
                           ValidationDisplayMode="ValidationDisplayMode.DescribedByWithHint" />

                <TimeInput class="br-col-xs-12 br-col-sm-6" LabelText="Start Work" @bind-Value="@_scheduleDataOne.StartWork" HintText="Optional, the time (24-hour format) you start work." Required="false"
                           EnableSeconds="false" DataPosition="DataPosition.Start" UpdateOnInput="true" ParseErrorMessage="If entered must be a valid time."
                           ValidationDisplayMode="ValidationDisplayMode.DescribedByWithHint" />

            </div>
            <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;">
                <button class="test-button" type="submit">Submit One to trigger validation on unmodified fields</button>
                <button @ref="ResetButtonOne" class="test-button" type="button" @onclick="ResetEditContextOne">Reset Example One</button>
            </div>
        </EditForm>

    </section>

